# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale fi
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as aamu [05:00, 10:00)
# (CLDR morning1).
# Surface: aamulla, the adessive of aamu "morning" -- the form a speaker
# uses adverbially; the bare nominative aamu is the citation form and is
# deliberately NOT shipped.
# Source: Wiktionary, "aamulla": Finnish adverb, glossed "at morning", and
# the adessive singular of "aamu".
# https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aamulla
# CLDR 47 fi names this period "aamulla" in the format-wide day periods,
# confirming the adessive is the surface, not the nominative.
aamulla
